     "type": "practice",
     "title": "Practice: The Synthetic Content Drill",
     "content": "**Goal**: build the provenance reflex for images, audio, and video — before you need it on something that matters.\n\n**Part 1 — The provenance trace (10 min)**: Find any striking image or clip currently circulating on social media (trending tabs are full of them). Now answer, in writing:\n1. What account posted the version I saw? Is it the originator or a resharer?\n2. Can I find the EARLIEST version? (Reverse image search helps for images; for video, search descriptions of the event plus the date.)\n3. Is the original poster identifiable and accountable — a named outlet, an official account, a verifiable witness? Or anonymous?\n4. Do independent established sources report the same event? With the same framing, or different context?\n5. Verdict: established provenance / unclear provenance / traces to an unaccountable single origin.\n\nDo this for three pieces of content. You'll find at least one where the trail dead-ends at an anonymous account — and that 'striking image with no provenance' is precisely the profile of synthetic or miscontextualized content.\n\n**Part 2 — The miscontextualization hunt (5 min)**: Most visual misinformation is NOT AI-generated. It's REAL footage from a different time, place, or event, relabeled. (A 2015 flood becomes 'last night's storm'; a military exercise becomes 'the invasion beginning.') This is cheaper than deepfakes and works just as well. For one of your three items, specifically ask: even if this footage is authentic, is the CAPTION's claim about when/where/what actually supported? Footage authenticates itself; captions never do.\n\n**Part 3 — The personal stakes inventory (5 min)**: Write down the two or three scenarios where synthetic content could actually hurt YOU or your family: a cloned voice calling about an emergency and asking for money; a fake message from your 'bank'; fabricated content about someone you know. For each, write the verification step NOW, while calm: a family code word for emergency calls; calling the bank back on the number on your card; contacting the person directly before believing content about them. Pre-deciding the protocol is what makes it available under stress — exactly Lesson 1's lesson, brought home.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\">\n                    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">PRACTICE: SYNTHETIC CONTENT</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Build the provenance reflex before you need it</text>\n                    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"170\" width=\"900\" height=\"280\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.12)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"220\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">PART 1: TRACE THREE ITEMS (10 min)</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"270\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Earliest version? Reverse image search.</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"310\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Originator identifiable — or anonymous?</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"350\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Independent outlets reporting the same event?</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"395\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Striking content + no provenance =</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"425\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">the exact profile of synthetic/miscontextualized media</text>\n                    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"480\" width=\"900\" height=\"240\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"530\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">PART 2: THE CHEAPER TRICK (5 min)</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"580\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Most visual misinformation is REAL footage,</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"615\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">relabeled: wrong time, wrong place, wrong event</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"660\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">2015 flood → \"last night's storm\"</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"695\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Footage authenticates itself; captions never do</text>\n                    <rect x=\"100\" y=\"750\" width=\"900\" height=\"290\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"800\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">PART 3: PERSONAL STAKES (5 min)</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"850\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Cloned voice \"emergency\" call → family code word</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"890\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">\"Bank\" message → call back the number on your card</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"930\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">Content about someone you know → ask them directly</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"975\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Pre-decide the protocol while calm —</text>\n                    <text x=\"550\" y=\"1005\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">stress will not let you invent it on the spot</text>\n                </svg>",
      "caption": "Trace it, question the caption, pre-decide the protocol"
     }
